{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793583523255067001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"golden-convergent-boutu","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"db522837bc35d0f2fcfe09dbabd5c7f7646ba06b65a8d8d30eb7694cfb6d3587","event_uuid":"730c2562-bf00-4439-b5b0-d171539f446b","position":{"commit_sha":"64978f2020704ecf3e8117755722f5f8c15a1528","position":"1793578986361911586-730c2562-bf00-4439-b5b0-d171539f446b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d732a265cd6285e4085cbc9bd1e15344b25658a1b4c032474febda363abe2960","event_uuid":"24a8a815-6d3e-4839-91df-7498161254dc","position":{"commit_sha":"82184ed3f732272d7f12841edaceb9c2aab5fbbc","position":"1793579011368607774-24a8a815-6d3e-4839-91df-7498161254dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"11a0e131863ccccc132292336de26df74e33ef731010e3361aa68ab9029fa1bf","event_uuid":"67c44353-b014-4b2c-b3d0-15374435466a","position":{"commit_sha":"7b8f8a4343b479622cbaca55a863abbc2efc1279","position":"1793579501814531723-67c44353-b014-4b2c-b3d0-15374435466a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2f41a47eb9be933279d8e47a774d602da2b7f899864d50475fc94d522739c4ff","event_uuid":"9761a809-8e69-4f3e-a99a-45afae149763","position":{"commit_sha":"eb4d733b1daf812843465cac8c943b1edaaffa86","position":"1793581553557400839-9761a809-8e69-4f3e-a99a-45afae149763"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"6f7237056b4e11d54049d14bfdfc307458b8ec14e9eab47d1149784bebe7f52a","event_uuid":"fbd2f41a-ea17-4dce-bd81-506866566606","position":{"commit_sha":"89fb00a7a8b1c4c0203a743214891a68fa9be39a","position":"1793581576577333706-fbd2f41a-ea17-4dce-bd81-506866566606"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793578986361911586,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"24a8a815-6d3e-4839-91df-7498161254dc","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe lexical tier reaches semantic recall@5 0.823. ADR 0122 measured one candidate that beats it distinguishably at k=5: `vector` — a Haiku-written digest of each ticket, embedded and ranked by cosine similarity — at 0.876, McNemar p=0.0213, recovering 13 pairs and losing 3. That single comparison is the entire justification for this tier, and it is worth 93 otherwise-invisible duplicate pairs on this store.\n\nrebar runs against diverse model providers, so this tier must not be reachable through one vendor only. It must also not become a dependency the feature cannot survive: an installation with no provider at all still needs similar-ticket surfacing to work.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Portability is delivered by the lexical tier, not by this one.** The index sibling ships retrieval, and the surfacing sibling ships the advisory, with no provider, no credentials and no network between them. That is what makes similar-ticket surfacing available in every installation. This tier is an opt-in ranking upgrade that requires *some* embedding provider, and the feature degrades to lexical whenever one is absent or failing. Stating it that way is what keeps the portability claim true; a tier that needs a provider cannot honestly be described as credential-free.\n\n**Vendor-neutrality comes from a seam rebar's runtime already ships.** pydantic-ai 1.107.9 — already the LLM runtime behind `src/rebar/llm/providers.py` — exposes a first-class embeddings API (`Embedder`, `EmbeddingModel`, `EmbeddingResult`, `EmbeddingSettings`, `infer_embedding_model`, `KnownEmbeddingModelName`) with provider backends for `bedrock`, `openai`, `cohere`, `google`, `voyageai` and `sentence_transformers`, plus `OpenAIEmbeddingsCompatibleProvider` for arbitrary OpenAI-compatible endpoints. Dispatching a `provider:model` string through `infer_embedding_model` is the same shape `providers.py` already uses for chat models, so this tier is a configured model name over an existing seam rather than a new provider abstraction. No vendor is reachable in a way the others are not.\n\n**No new runtime dependency is taken.** `pydantic_ai.embeddings.sentence_transformers` imports numpy and raises `ImportError` directing the user to the optional `pydantic-ai-slim[sentence-transformers]` group; it is not installed in this checkout, and the backend downloads model weights on first use. A fully local backend is therefore available to an operator who installs that group, but rebar does not take the dependency and this ticket does not claim an offline embedding path. Offline operation is the lexical tier's job.\n\n**Configured default.** `bedrock:amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0`, 1,024 dimensions, cosine — the model ADR 0122 measured. It is a default, not a requirement.\n\n**Digest step.** `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0`, the 4-field prompt pinned at commit `f147e08242f`, input capped at 40,000 characters, per ADR 0122's architecture section. The digest is kept despite being the weakest link, and the plan states why rather than hiding it: `vector` is *not* distinguishable from `vector-raw`, which skips the digest (p=0.0654 and p=0.0625). The digest survives only because `vector-raw` also fails to beat `fts5` (p=0.6636) — a non-transitive chain ADR 0122 states plainly. Dropping the digest cannot be justified from the current evidence, and neither can a strong claim that it helps.\n\n**Two counters ADR 0122 makes mandatory for any consumer.** Its Consequences section records that the digest parser silently returned empty fields for three distinct reply shapes, each indistinguishable from success without an `empties` counter; and that 2 of 630 tickets did not answer the task at all, both succeeding on retry, which makes retry the correct handling rather than a workaround. A consumer that omits either reproduces a defect already diagnosed.\n\n**Ranking swaps behind an interface that already has a working implementation.** The index, its dir-hash freshness map and read-phase catch-up come from the index sibling; the advisory across all four create surfaces comes from the surfacing sibling. This tier replaces only the scoring function and adds the digest-and-embed build step. k stays at 5 — ADR 0122's decision is scoped to that operating point, and at k=10 `vector`'s semantic edge is indistinguishable (p=0.3438).\n\n**Tests use `TestEmbeddingModel`, and that is not evidence of portability.** pydantic-ai's test double makes the tier deterministic offline without mocking a vendor's wire format, which is the right way to test ranking behaviour. It is a test double, so it is used for behaviour tests only; the claim that a second real provider works is carried by a test that constructs a second provider's model through `infer_embedding_model` and asserts the dispatch, not by the double.\n\nAny ratcheted mechanism this tier adds — the embedding-model config key is the expected one — carries a `# mechanism-ok:` marker at its definition site naming this ticket, since `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` fails on any unadmitted new mechanism.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An embedding model configured as a `provider:model` string is resolved through pydantic-ai's `infer_embedding_model`, and retrieval ranks by cosine similarity over the resulting vectors. Checked by: a test configuring `TestEmbeddingModel` and asserting the returned ordering follows cosine similarity rather than the lexical score.\n- [ ] Configuring a model string for at least two distinct providers resolves to each provider's embedding model with no code change and no vendor branch in rebar. Checked by: a test parameterized over two provider-qualified model strings asserting `infer_embedding_model` returns the matching model class for each, skipping only on a missing optional dependency rather than passing vacuously.\n- [ ] With no embedding model configured, retrieval returns the lexical tier's results and the create exits 0. Checked by: a test asserting the advisory matches the lexical tier's output when the key is unset.\n- [ ] When the configured provider raises a denial, retrieval falls back to lexical-only with a diagnostic and the create exits 0. Checked by: a test asserting exit status, advisory contents and the diagnostic.\n- [ ] When the configured provider times out, retrieval falls back to lexical-only with a diagnostic and the create exits 0. Checked by: a test asserting exit status, advisory contents and the diagnostic.\n- [ ] When the digest reply parses to empty fields, retrieval falls back to lexical-only with a diagnostic and the create exits 0. Checked by: a test asserting exit status, advisory contents and the diagnostic.\n- [ ] An `empties` counter records every digest reply that parses to an empty field and is observable after an index build. Checked by: a test feeding each of the three reply shapes ADR 0122 records and asserting the counter equals 3 while the build still completes.\n- [ ] A digest reply that does not answer the task is retried, and a success on retry is recorded as a success. Checked by: a test whose model fails once then succeeds, asserting the ticket is indexed and the retry is counted.\n- [ ] rebar's installed runtime dependencies are unchanged by this ticket. Checked by: `pyproject.toml`'s dependency lists are untouched in the diff.\n- [ ] Every module added or modified under `src/rebar/` is at most 800 lines. Checked by: the CI module-size gate.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0, with any new mechanism admitted by a `# mechanism-ok:` marker naming this ticket. Checked by: running it.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exits 0. Checked by: running it.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/similar/embedding.py","reason":"new opt-in embedding tier: digest step, infer_embedding_model dispatch, cosine ranking"},{"path":"src/rebar/similar/index.py","reason":"ranking function swaps behind the existing interface; vector storage on build"},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"embedding-model config key, admitted by a mechanism-ok marker"},{"path":"tests/test_similar_tickets_embedding.py","reason":"ranking, two-provider dispatch, degradation, empties counter and retry tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","47c8-97ac-eff3-4e88"],["parent","4e89-30b9-1666-4e53"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"4e89-30b9-1666-4e53","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_id":"2041-75d6-2a2f-4be9","ticket_type":"story","title":"Add an opt-in embedding retrieval tier over pydantic-ai's provider-agnostic embeddings seam","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["730c2562-bf00-4439-b5b0-d171539f446b","24a8a815-6d3e-4839-91df-7498161254dc","67c44353-b014-4b2c-b3d0-15374435466a","9761a809-8e69-4f3e-a99a-45afae149763","fbd2f41a-ea17-4dce-bd81-506866566606"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793583523255067001,"uuid":"267d4b8a-2c04-42c6-bcbf-a833bea16d50"}